  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two individuals: one who was banned for criticizing a movie, and another who promoted a hoax hate crime that risked an entire race war, yet remains on Twitter. The intent is to highlight perceived double standards or hypocrisy in platform moderation, suggesting that the platform allows harmful content while punishing criticism. This can be interpreted as harmful because it may normalize or justify the spread of dangerous misinformation by implying that the consequences for promoting such content are negligible compared to the punishment for criticism. The meme uses the contrast to provoke outrage or debate, potentially reinforcing harmful narratives about online accountability and racial tensions.",
